SUMMARY:A Day in the Life of a Pathologist: The Science That Shapes Health
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260626T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260626T130000
DTSTAMP:20260606T100710Z
UID:9f720d950325ee3e45edba071a592333@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:museum,science,family,all_audiences
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Field Museum - Events\\nAges: All ages\\nCategory: 
 General\\n\\nVisit the Grainger Science Hub and meet scientists from the C
 ollege of American Pathologists to  explore the role of a pathologist and
  examine its impact on overall health. This interactive drop-in experience
  will introduce the world of pathology through hands-on observation\, patt
 ern recognition\, and diagnostic thinking. Visitors will rotate through st
 ations that mirror the work pathologists do every day: examining tissues\,
  identifying disease patterns\, comparing healthy and abnormal samples\, a
 nd using clues to determine diagnoses. Discover how pathology is the “de
 tective work” of medicine\, combining science\, visual analytics\, and c
 lassification to understand disease.\\n\\nMore info: https://www.fieldmuse
 um.org/our-events/meet-a-scientist/a-day-in-the-life-of-a-pathologist-the-
 science-that-shapes-health
LOCATION:Field Museum\, 1400 S Lake Shore Dr\, Chicago\, IL 60605
URL:https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/meet-a-scientist/a-day-in-the-l
 ife-of-a-pathologist-the-science-that-shapes-health
