BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dust from the Cosmos
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260701T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260701T130000
DTSTAMP:20260606T100710Z
UID:fdc398c1a3684eaff44d90e2a72941b0@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:museum,science,family,all_audiences
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Field Museum - Events\\nCost: Included with admissi
 on\\nAges: All ages\\nCategory: General\\n\\nVisit the Grainger Science Hu
 b to see micrometeorites found on the roof of the Field Museum! Explore ho
 w cosmic dust can be found everywhere - from the rooftops of buildings to 
 the deserts of Antarctica. Touch meteorites that are 4.5 billion years old
  and observe how a Scanning Electron Microscope can be used to identify mi
 crometeorites. This session will be presented by Basil Saleem\, Resident G
 raduate Student\, Field Museum. --\\n\\nMore info: https://www.fieldmuseum
